#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfd612a0-8d9c-551c-a83d-74c0e3cc77e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{3}{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351031} {:answer/id #uuid "d28bdea0-7ab5-5903-8698-20f181cb2809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{3}{v}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351032} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9f6a1b-525a-5554-a40b-8b6a28f43944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{4}{v}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351033} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5a051a-6f4f-589f-b410-0ec4c3589f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351034} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4154ce-01ce-5b7b-87c6-a5a74439cad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b5a051a-6f4f-589f-b410-0ec4c3589f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351034} :answer-field/id #uuid "50efa88f-c9c6-5856-bb71-fac8d3cbf20b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c502543-bf1e-5bea-aad2-6cc3e7e40f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-161134" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =({u}^{2}\\cdot {u}^{2})\\cdot {v}^{2}\\cdot {v}^{2}\\, \\\\  & ={u}^{4}{v}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
